    "updated_at": "2022-02-12T03:52:58Z",
    "body": "I started looking at #2010 for inspiration and realized that it allows me to do what I want with config alone. In addition to `repo_root_style` that's documented, there's an undocumented `repo_root_format` option that does actually separate the path into its component parts. With this new config, I can get exactly what I want, for any arbitrary git repo. I just had to remove the `$repo_root` section from the `repo_root_format`.\r\n\r\n```\r\n[directory]\r\ntruncate_to_repo = true\r\nrepo_root_format = \"[$before_root_path]($style)[$path]($style)\"\r\nrepo_root_style = \"\"\r\n```\r\n\r\nSo I'm going to close this ticket, and if someone is so inclined, they can decide whether to document the `repo_root_format` configuration option for folks like me who can make use of it.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
